-a4b1a66521e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447465 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447470 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447470 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37357" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447470 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-40 & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a82c548a-99d5-5982-b67f-c8bf62fc70fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447470 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 30 \\\\ -80 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )((-40-\\lambda )(60-\\lambda )-(30)(-80)) & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda )(\\lambda -20) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447472 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447472 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447472 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447472 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447472 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bca3e3e8-22f6-5c69-8cd2-18d06e6e998f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447472 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447473 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447473 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86751" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447473 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447473 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447473 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d00c6bd7-a884-5180-8cfd-0ffa34fc590f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447473 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(E-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
